WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.540
Amazing! Showtime!

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.390
My HOT teacher activities,

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.940
Aikatsu! is ready to start! Yeah!

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.290
My name is Johnny Bepp.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.470
The number one teacher in the galaxy. 
My entire life is a showtime!

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.580
I dance and groove to my heart's rhythm and beat.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:26.840
This humble story is about a certain cool teacher and his honeys ever aiming for top idol.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.570
It's a burning hot success story.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:30.710
Bepp-sensei.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.190
Oh, Headmistress.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.660
Just because it's April Fools doesn't mean you can get so high and mighty.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.970
Sorry.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.340
Hi, signalize!

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.720
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.700
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.590
No, that's wrong

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.590
iie chigau yo

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:08.970
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:08.970
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.760
Do that signalize!

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.940
Something's starting to bubble up

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.940
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.900
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.900
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:23.440
So I'll believe in the present

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:23.440
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.610
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.610
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.950
Chance for me

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:35.250
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:35.250
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:39.460
It's just another challenge on the way

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:39.460
hora chousen matteru yo

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:44.380
Where are we headed?

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:44.380
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:48.130
Into a brilliant hope

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:48.130
mabushii kibou no naka e

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:55.390
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:55.390
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:58.770
Where we're headed

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:58.770
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.650
is into our hopes for the future

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.650
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:09.990
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:09.990
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.360
I'm home!

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.450
Dad, welcome back!

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.770
Geez, that text came out of nowhere.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.340
You always surprise us like that.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.010
Hey, sorry about that.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.170
I just wanted to see everyone's surprised faces.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.460
You <i>bet</i> we were surprised! I thought 
it was an April Fools joke up till now.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.320
April Fools?

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.180
Oh yeah, today's April 1st!

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.550
I've been flying around the skies so 
long I've lost track of what day it is.  {I think you need to do too much thinking to ascertain airplanes from "in the air"}

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.710
At least your feet are firmly on the ground now, Taichi-kun. How does a meal sound?

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.510
Looks like my stomach got the first word in.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.940
I was so excited to eat your home cooking that I didn't eat on the plane at all.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.190
Then it seems as though I've got to answer those expectations.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:01.530
I'll help out too.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.210
Oh boy, I can hardly wait now.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.900
Raichi, want to try doing "that" again?

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.960
What? But I'm not a little kid anymore.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.140
Here we go!

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.340
Hang on tight, buddy! Papa express, go!

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.110
It's like he never even left. {yeah, I don't think a literal translation works}

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:21.220
I agree.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.470
Thanks for the food.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.600
That's more like it—nothing like a Japanese breakfast.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.170
Great!

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.560
Your miso soup's the best in the world, Ringo.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.970
I'm the one who fried the fish.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.490
I only burnt it a little... is it bad?

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.610
Delicious!

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:48.000
Ichigo, you sure have grown since I've been away.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.710
Dad, your fish's going to get salty. {I have to admit, this joke was too high level for me the first couple times}

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.380
Sorry about that, I was just so moved.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.320
That's an exaggeration.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.880
It's so fluffy and warm!

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:06.180
Looks like you really did inherit Dad's love of food.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.600
Really? You think so?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.290
So good.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.890
Yeah, this really is the best.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.400
Yeah, I guess you're right!

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.110
Thanks for the meal.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.130
I'm glad you all liked it.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:23.400
Hey, Dad. What kind of adventure 
did you have this time?

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.410
He's not adventuring, he's working.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.660
Though it sure does feel like an adventure from time to time.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:36.670
I travel around the world looking for delicious flavors no one knows about.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.630
So, this time...

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.170
What happened?

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.180
I heard a rumor that there was a miraculous fruit hidden deep within the jungle.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:47.430
I was fighting my way through the 
dense thicket, when suddenly...

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.310
A starving puma appeared before my eyes!

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.310
I started running for my life, when...!

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.830
I found a river! {~kawa ga nagareru~}

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.570
I jumped in without looking,

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:04.070
and tried to swim to the other side, but...!

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:07.890
An uncountable number of crocodiles came out of the water

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.620
opening their mouths as if to eat me in one gulp!

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:17.330
But then I leapt onto their backs and jump, jump, jumped!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.080
Somehow I managed to make it to the other side.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.240
Wow!

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.210
But man, that was dangerous, even for me.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.600
But you made it back in one piece.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:34.350
And then what? Did you find the miraculous fruit?

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.850
You bet I did!

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.560
They look like stars!

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.640
They're called "stargrapes".

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.220
Go ahead and try one.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:50.870
Sure!

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:54.640
It's great!

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:56.190
It's so sweet!

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.120
Really? Then me too...

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:03.750
Just tasting it fills me with happiness.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:07.960
It's a miraculous fruit that can make anyone smile.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:11.840
I went all around the jungle searching, and I eventually found them, but...

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.360
Stargrapes belong to this village alone!

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.520
I won't allow them outside this land!

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:20.310
Please reconsider.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:23.390
I want to use these fruits to bring 
smiles to everyone in the world. {wow, a legitimate}{??}

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:24.230
Leave!

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:25.780
I will not.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:32.450
I asked him over and over after that,

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.430
but he never once allowed me to take them.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:35.910
But what about these?

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:40.790
When I said I was going back to Japan, he gave me these as a special gift.

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.540
Is it okay for us to eat something so important? {this is how I interpreted these lines, but it produces awkwardly long lines and is questionably correct. make your judgement.}

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.310
It's <i>because</i> it's important that I want you to eat it.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.700
More than anything in the world,
 I wanted to see your smiles.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.960
Dad...

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:56.430
Dad, look. This was my first movie.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.360
Stylish Thieves Swallowtail!

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:02.400
Though we may look sweet, we're burning with spice!

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:07.250
I heard about it from Ringo before,

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:10.200
but you really are an idol now, Ichigo.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.780
Yeah, Onee-chan's amazing! 
But even more amazing than her is...

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.740
Aoi-neesan!

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.060
Oh, Ichigo's friend.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:21.360
I see you're an Aoi-chan fan then.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.080
Yeah!

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:26.010
The two of them are shining more brightly every day.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.600
You think so?

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:31.590
Oh, right. How long are you home this time, Dad?

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:34.720
Let's see, probably until the end of spring break.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:39.430
Great! I'm going to be in a live audition
 on the last day of spring break.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.580
No way I could let that chance pass me by.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:46.110
I want to burn your shining figure into the back of my eyes.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:50.200
Thanks! I'll try my best to show you 
the best performance ever!

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:54.670
It's from Aoi.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:55.870
Aoi-neesan?

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:00.040
We're starting practice for our next audition at noon.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.220
Let's do our best!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.830
I've gotta get going soon.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:06.500
I wanted to talk a little more though...

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:11.470
This is a rare opportunity, so I think I'll go give my 
regards to the people looking after Ichigo.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.880
Dad!

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:16.520
Now nice, I wanna hang out with Dad too.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:20.320
As soon as I'm done at Ichigo's 
school I'll play with you all you want.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:20.850
'Kay?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.770
Okay, it's a promise!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:23.990
You bet.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.940
Thank you for looking after my daughter.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:33.450
Hoshimiya-san's efforts have really caught our attention.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.660
She's one of our most promising students right now.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.830
Isn't that right, Bepp-sensei?

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:39.700
Yes.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.960
I'm Starmiya's teacher, Johnny.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.900
Hoshimiya Taichi.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.080
I leave my daughter's education in your hands.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:52.920
<i>Hoshimiya Taichi... he is...</i>

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:54.090
<i>...quite the man. {hmm}</i>

00:08:57.110 --> 00:09:00.850
I should've expected Hime-chan to be the same old cool beauty as always.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:01.900
"Hime-chan"?

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.190
Right, I guess I should be calling her "Headmistress" now.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.910
I'm just so used to her other name.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:10.230
Did you use to be a fan of Masquerade?

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:14.650
I was. Everyone was really into Masquerade back then.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:15.990
Wow.

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:24.660
Nice to meet you! I'm Ichigo's number one fan, Kiriya Aoi. {nice intro} {an ichigo pun that doesn't involve strawberries;}

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.170
Thank you for letting me observe your practice today.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:37.180
The next audition will be done live in this five-girl formation. {switched out man for girl}

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:41.270
In order to pass, you're going to need to be completely in sync with each other. {the sync vs. synch debate is an interesting one, and from an ideological standpoint I do like synch better, but sync looks better and is more widely accepted, so...}

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.330
I'm sorry!

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:45.560
You got too close.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.810
You were one beat too late too, Yurika.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.890
How could you possibly tell?

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.470
Could you have used the powers of darkness...

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:55.070
I could tell by listening to your footsteps.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.880
Don't worry, we've practiced this over and over.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:03.670
Let's just try to unite our hearts and imagine how everyone else is moving.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.770
Sounds good.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.250
Right! Imagine, imagine!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.440
They're amazing.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.720
What do you think of this team?

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:15.840
Let me think...

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.850
Though their personalities are all different and it seems like they wouldn't work well together,

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:26.830
when they combine their efforts
 they make a truly wonderful team.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.730
Yes!

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.680
Dad, how was it?

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:48.540
You girls sure were great.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:52.810
It really is all that unseen effort that 
makes a truly great concert. {good enough}

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.800
Yurika-chan, you're going home already?

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.680
That's right. I've spent too much time being stained by the sun.

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.890
I need to go recover my powers of darkness.

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:02.800
Powers of darkness?

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.330
I'm Toudou Yurika.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:08.640
I'm a descendant of the great Count Dracula.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:12.900
But instead of an introduction,
 perhaps I should suck your blood?

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.040
My blood?

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:14.900
Um...

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.410
That's her character.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:18.390
What a great opportunity!

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:22.030
I never expected to find a vampire way out in Japan!

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:28.160
I haven't been this impressed since I 
met a yeti out in the Himalayas.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.010
Before you suck my blood, may I shake your hand?

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:32.740
O-Of course.

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:34.460
A yeti?

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.240
Not a chance.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.720
Yeti-tan... {halp} {no}

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.400
Love you!

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:50.110
Dad, why don't you tell Otome-chan about the time you made friends with a bear?

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:51.480
With a bear?!

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.730
Sure, why not.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:58.110
It was when I was in the Arctic— 
I ran into a starving polar bear.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:02.200
He was in really bad shape, so I split this food called "pemmican" with him.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.620
He got really attached to me after that...

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.980
He brought you all the way to your destination, right?

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:11.240
He really saved me back there.
 I would've gotten lost without him.

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:17.400
Otome wants to become friends with a bear too!

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:21.130
Love you!

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:24.470
Not a chance! Real polar bears are like <i>this</i>!

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.270
What's going on?

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:29.950
I know, who would've though he'd accept your vampire character so quickly.

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:33.890
That's not what I mean! I'm talking 
about the yeti and polar bear stuff.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:34.900
Could it be?

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.650
What's up, Aoi?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.790
Today's the first of April.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:40.630
You mean April Fools day?

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:41.650
Oh, it's that...

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:45.530
Well then, Ichigo. I'll be looking 
forward to your live audition.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.160
Thanks.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.280
Be sure to come. It's a promise, okay?

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.290
You bet.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.700
We're home!

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.180
What happened to you two?

00:12:55.180 --> 00:13:00.180
Well you know, I was playing soccer with Raichi and his friends and I just got really into it.

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:01.830
Dad was amazing.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.880
He made a diving catch every time we shot a ball at him!

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:08.190
The bath is ready, so head on in.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.410
Sure. Dad, wanna go together?

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:13.100
Sounds good, it's time for a father and son bath!

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:13.680
Great!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.850
Alright, let's jump on in there!

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.020
Dad sure hasn't changed a bit.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:25.790
Good work today.

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:26.940
Where are the kids?

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:28.280
Both sleeping soundly.

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:32.480
And that is?

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:35.790
It's a picture I took with the village kids.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:38.440
There's no school in their village.

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:42.800
They have to walk several hours though the dangerous jungle just to get to one.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.340
That's so harsh...

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:47.500
But if I'm able to bring stargrape fruit to the world,

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:51.010
then I might be able to build a school 
in the village with the money.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:54.960
I love the people of that village.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:58.190
Though it'll probably be hard to get the elder's permission to do what I want.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.430
I'm sure your feelings will get though.

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.900
You can definitely do it.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.400
Hello...

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:12.410
Right... okay...

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.340
The elder said that?

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:17.850
<i>Yeah, he said it's alright to take stargrapes from the village.</i>

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:19.040
<i>You sure did it, Hoshimiya.</i>

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.340
That's great.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:23.070
<i>I'm sorry to spring this on you, but...</i>

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.050
<i>Think you could go back right away?</i>

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:29.190
<i>The Elder says he wants to talk to you as soon as possible.</i>

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:31.340
"As soon as possible"?

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:35.210
<i>You know how quickly his mood changes better than anyone.</i>

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.480
<i>You need to get back before he changes his mind.</i>

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.940
I understand.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:50.490
Have a safe trip.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:51.950
I'm off.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.880
Do your best at work.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.870
I'll do the same for my audition.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:58.750
You bet. I'll be cheering for you too.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:14:59.960
Thanks!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.460
Please take me to the airport.

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:13.470
What?

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.760
But that means her dad can't...

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:19.330
Right. He's going to the other side of the world.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.540
No matter how much he hurries...

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.900
There's no way he can make it back for the audition.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:28.650
But why? He was looking forward to it so much...

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:31.660
April Fools. {what are you even doing}

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:35.160
Forget about the yeti and bear parts...

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.410
<i>Be sure to come. It's a promise, okay?</i>

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:38.410
<i>You bet.</i>

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:44.270
I hope that those were the only lies he told.

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:46.000
Ichigo-tan...

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.760
Alright, here we go!

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:53.970
Let's combine all our feelings and pass that live audition!

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.330
Ichigo.

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.770
I know I told you to come immediately, but...

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.660
I never expected you to rush <i>this</i> much.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:07.270
There's a promise that I have to keep.

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.860
A promise?

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:16.930
Everyone, let's go put on the best concert we can.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.370
Yeah!

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:53.960
Melody Musical! {thanks for ruining the mood}

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:03.010
Dad! We passed the audition!

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.870
You did it, Ichigo!

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:09.430
I'm so surprised. How did you make it back so quickly?

00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:11.690
Is everything at your job okay?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.230
You bet, no need to worry.

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:15.980
You fool!

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.190
What?

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:20.470
Why didn't you mention the promise with your daughter?

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.980
I'll allow you to bring the stargrapes out of the village.

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:25.700
You just focus on getting back to 
your daughter as soon as you can!

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:27.370
Can I really?

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.380
Yes.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:31.470
"Treasure your family more than any gem."

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:33.870
That's a tradition passed on in our village for generations.

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:35.550
Elder...

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:38.670
I can tell just by looking at you.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:42.400
You'd go to any ends to keep the promise with your daughter.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:46.260
You're a man that I can place my trust in.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:52.480
Really? Thank you very much!

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:54.390
Dad...

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:59.020
You really <i>were</i> able to keep your promise.

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:02.340
Of course he did. Dad never lies after all.

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:06.320
That's right. Ever since we met, your father hasn't broken a single promise with me,

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:09.030
and he never tells any lies either.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:12.540
I think I can understand where Ichigo gets her straightforward personality from.

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:17.040
Aye. I'm certain that Ichigo-tan's 
house is always overflowing with love.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.040
You're right.

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:19.500
What's wrong?

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:22.730
They said that Ichigo's father has never told a lie.

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:24.050
But that means...

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:28.510
<i>I haven't been this impressed since I 
met a yeti out in the Himalayas.</i>

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:33.930
<i>It was when I was in the Arctic— 
I ran into a starving polar bear.</i>

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:36.690
It's the truth.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:39.120
My Dad would never tell a lie.

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:48.280
Your performance today was amazing.

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:52.290
I was able to make one last wonderful memory before leaving Japan again.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:58.170
No matter how far apart we may be,
 I'll always be cheering you on.

00:21:58.170 --> 00:21:59.460
I know.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:01.470
Then off I go!

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.430
Have a safe trip!

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:06.190
Take care of yourself!

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:07.090
Dad!

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:10.050
Until the next time you come home,

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:15.720
I'll work hard to become a top idol that can bring a smile to everyone's face!

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:19.350
Yeah, you can definitely do it!

00:23:55.640 --> 00:23:57.800
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:01.540
I want to meet a yeti so badly!

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:03.460
Do they even exist?

00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:05.340
But there's a vampire right in front of my eyes?

00:24:05.340 --> 00:24:06.680
Right...

00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:09.880
Truth is stranger than fiction.

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:11.780
Welcome, new students!

00:24:11.780 --> 00:24:15.470
Ichigo-sama, I humbly ask for your guidance in any matters to come.

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:17.810
N-Naish to meet you too!

00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:19.620
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:19.620 --> 00:24:21.080
The Season of Sakura. {name pun again}

00:24:21.080 --> 00:24:23.550
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
